le",{"title":144,"path":145,"stem":146,"icon":104},"SIEM export","\u002Fsecurity\u002Fsiem-export","5.security\u002F7.siem-export",{"title":148,"path":149,"stem":150,"icon":43},"Wazuh and Suricata","\u002Fsecurity\u002Fwazuh-suricata","5.security\u002F8.wazuh-suricata",{"title":152,"icon":153,"path":154,"stem":155,"children":156,"page":49},"Reference","i-lucide-book-marked","\u002Freference","6.reference",[157,162,167,172,177],{"title":158,"path":159,"stem":160,"icon":161},"Agent protocol","\u002Freference\u002Fprotocol","6.reference\u002F1.protocol","i-lucide-arrow-left-right",{"title":163,"path":164,"stem":165,"icon":166},"UI API","\u002Freference\u002Fui-api","6.reference\u002F2.ui-api","i-lucide-braces",{"title":168,"path":169,"stem":170,"icon":171},"Metric storage","\u002Freference\u002Fmetric-storage","6.reference\u002F3.metric-storage","i-lucide-database",{"title":173,"path":174,"stem":175,"icon":176},"Performance","\u002Freference\u002Fperformance","6.reference\u002F4.performance","i-lucide-gauge",{"title":178,"path":179,"stem":180,"icon":181},"Development","\u002Freference\u002Fdevelopment","6.reference\u002F5.development","i-lucide-code",{"title":183,"path":184,"stem":185,"children":186,"icon":189},"Internals","\u002Finternals","7.internals\u002F1.index",[187,190,195,199,204,208],{"title":188,"path":184,"stem":185,"icon":189},"Frappe Cloud v2, read from its code","i-lucide-map",{"title":191,"path":192,"stem":193,"icon":194},"The applications","\u002Finternals\u002Fapps","7.internals\u002F2.apps","i-lucide-boxes",{"title":196,"path":197,"stem":198,"icon":132},"Calls and trust","\u002Finternals\u002Finterop","7.internals\u002F3.interop",{"title":200,"path":201,"stem":202,"icon":203},"Flows","\u002Finternals\u002Fflows","7.internals\u002F4.flows","i-lucide-route",{"title":205,"path":206,"stem":207,"icon":38},"Inside a customer server","\u002Finternals\u002Fcustomer-server","7.internals\u002F5.customer-server",{"title":209,"path":210,"stem":211,"icon":117},"Notes for Wolf","\u002Finternals\u002Fwolf","7.internals\u002F6.wolf",{"id":213,"title":119,"body":214,"description":946,"extension":947,"links":948,"meta":949,"navigation":950,"path":120,"seo":951,"stem":121,"__hash__":952},"docs_en\u002F5.security\u002F2.site-signals.md",{"type":215,"value":216,"toc":930},"minimark",[217,226,233,238,244,371,387,410,414,420,593,596,602,606,612,684,687,693,710,713,727,744,748,764,768,781,837,846,849,852,857,917,920,924],[218,219,220,221,225],"p",{},"The site running Dodock Wolf records its own signals from Frappe's documents and requests. No\nagent is needed. Each signal has a switch in ",[222,223,224],"strong",{},"Wolf Settings",", and all are on by default.",[218,227,228,229,232],{},"These signals are only seen from inside a site. To get them for the other sites of a bench,\ninstall the Wolf App on each one in satellite mode: it captures the same signals, with the same\nswitches, and forwards them to the central site. See ",[230,231,40],"a",{"href":41},".",[234,235,237],"h2",{"id":236},"logins-and-roles","Logins and roles",[218,239,240,243],{},[222,241,242],{},"Wolf Settings → Local signals (this site)",":",[245,246,247,269],"table",{},[248,249,250],"thead",{},[251,252,253,257,260,263,266],"tr",{},[254,255,256],"th",{},"Setting",[254,258,259],{},"Category",[254,261,262],{},"What it records",[254,264,265],{},"Severity",[254,267,268],{},"Preset",[270,271,272,299,321,348],"tbody",{},[251,273,274,280,286,289,292],{},[275,276,277],"td",{},[222,278,279],{},"Capture failed logins",[275,281,282],{},[283,284,285],"code",{},"frappe_failed_login",[275,287,288],{},"a failed desk login (Activity Log), with the user and IP",[275,290,291],{},"warning",[275,293,294,298],{},[295,296,297],"em",{},"Repeated failed Frappe logins",": 5+ in 10 min, per site",[251,300,301,306,311,314,316],{},[275,302,303],{},[222,304,305],{},"Flag privileged logins from new IPs",[275,307,308],{},[283,309,310],{},"new_admin_ip",[275,312,313],{},"a privileged user logs in from an IP none of their earlier logins came from",[275,315,291],{},[275,317,318],{},[295,319,320],{},"Admin login from new IP",[251,322,323,328,333,340,343],{},[275,324,325],{},[222,326,327],{},"Flag privileged logins from new countries",[275,329,330],{},[283,331,332],{},"admin_login_new_country",[275,334,335,336],{},"a privileged login from a country none of the user's earlier logins came from. Needs a ",[230,337,339],{"href":338},"#geoip-database","GeoIP database",[275,341,342],{},"critical",[275,344,345],{},[295,346,347],{},"Admin login from new country",[251,349,350,355,360,363,366],{},[275,351,352],{},[222,353,354],{},"Flag users granted privileged roles",[275,356,357],{},[283,358,359],{},"privileged_user",[275,361,362],{},"an enabled user receives a privileged role",[275,364,365],{},"critical for System Manager or Administrator, else warning",[275,367,368],{},[295,369,370],{},"Privileged role granted",[218,372,373,376,377,380,381,380,384,232],{},[222,374,375],{},"Privileged Roles"," lists the roles that count as privileged, one per line. Default:\n",[283,378,379],{},"System Manager",", ",[283,382,383],{},"Administrator",[283,385,386],{},"Wolf Manager",[218,388,389,390,393,394,397,398,401,402,405,406,409],{},"The same section holds the non-security local signals: ",[222,391,392],{},"Capture failed Scheduled Job Logs","\n(",[283,395,396],{},"cron_failure",") and ",[222,399,400],{},"Capture Error Logs"," (failed backups as ",[283,403,404],{},"backup_failed","). ",[222,407,408],{},"Watch the Email\nQueue"," records Email Queue backlogs and sending errors.",[234,411,413],{"id":412},"risky-application-changes","Risky application changes",[218,415,416,419],{},[222,417,418],{},"Wolf Settings → Flag risky application changes"," (on by default) covers:",[245,421,422,436],{},[248,423,424],{},[251,425,426,428,431,434],{},[254,427,259],{},[254,429,430],{},"What raises it",[254,432,433],{},"ATT&CK",[254,435,268],{},[270,437,438,457,475,492,514,536,555,575],{},[251,439,440,445,448,451],{},[275,441,442],{},[283,443,444],{},"server_script_change",[275,446,447],{},"a Server Script created, enabled, or with its code, type or trigger changed",[275,449,450],{},"T1059.006",[275,452,453,456],{},[295,454,455],{},"Server Script can run new code"," (the event is critical for API and scheduled scripts or guest access)",[251,458,459,464,467,470],{},[275,460,461],{},[283,462,463],{},"client_script_change",[275,465,466],{},"the same for a Client Script",[275,468,469],{},"T1059.007",[275,471,472],{},[295,473,474],{},"Client Script can run new code",[251,476,477,482,485,487],{},[275,478,479],{},[283,480,481],{},"console_execution",[275,483,484],{},"each System Console run (Python or SQL)",[275,486,450],{},[275,488,489],{},[295,490,491],{},"System Console used",[251,493,494,499,506,509],{},[275,495,496],{},[283,497,498],{},"permission_change",[275,500,501,502],{},"see ",[230,503,505],{"href":504},"#permission-drift","Permission drift",[275,507,508],{},"T1098",[275,510,511],{},[295,512,513],{},"Permission rules changed",[251,515,516,521,527,530],{},[275,517,518],{},[283,519,520],{},"security_settings_weakened",[275,522,501,523],{},[230,524,526],{"href":525},"#weakened-settings","Weakened settings",[275,528,529],{},"T1562.001",[275,531,532,535],{},[295,533,534],{},"Security settings weakened"," (critical)",[251,537,538,543,546,549],{},[275,539,540],{},[283,541,542],{},"api_key_generated",[275,544,545],{},"a new API secret written for a user",[275,547,548],{},"T1098.001",[275,550,551,554],{},[295,552,553],{},"API key generated"," (the event is critical for privileged users)",[251,556,557,562,568,571],{},[275,558,559],{},[283,560,561],{},"api_key_new_ip",[275,563,501,564],{},[230,565,567],{"href":566},"#api-key-used-from-a-new-ip","API key used from a new IP",[275,569,570],{},"T1078, T1552",[275,572,573],{},[295,574,567],{},[251,576,577,582,585,588],{},[275,578,579],{},[283,580,581],{},"webhook_external",[275,583,584],{},"a Webhook created, enabled or pointed at another host",[275,586,587],{},"T1567",[275,589,590],{},[295,591,592],{},"Webhook to a new host",[218,594,595],{},"Editing a script's description or disabling a script raises nothing.",[597,598,599],"caution",{},[218,600,601],{},"Script events keep the first 300 characters of the code. A script that holds a secret puts part\nof it in the event.",[603,604,505],"h3",{"id":605},"permission-drift",[218,607,608,609,611],{},"All of these are ",[283,610,498],{}," events:",[613,614,615,633,658,668,678],"ul",{},[616,617,618,621,622,380,625,628,629,632],"li",{},[222,619,620],{},"Role Permission Manager",": add, update, remove and reset. Older Frappe versions write\n",[283,623,624],{},"update",[283,626,627],{},"remove"," and ",[283,630,631],{},"reset"," with raw SQL, so Wolf reads them from the request.",[616,634,635,638,639,642,643,380,646,649,650,653,654,657],{},[222,636,637],{},"Custom DocPerm"," saved or deleted anywhere else: Data Import, the REST API, code\n(",[283,640,641],{},"payload.kind"," is ",[283,644,645],{},"custom_docperm",[283,647,648],{},"via"," says how). Each event lists the rights granted and\nremoved. A new rule is compared with the DocType's standard rule, so the copies Frappe makes\nbefore the first custom change grant nothing. A right given to ",[283,651,652],{},"Guest"," or ",[283,655,656],{},"All"," is critical.",[616,659,660,663,664,667],{},[222,661,662],{},"User Permission"," that lets its user see more (",[283,665,666],{},"user_permission","). The first User Permission\nof a user for a DocType only restricts and raises nothing. A further value, an edit that allows\nanother value, user or DocType, or removing the last one (which lifts the restriction) raises an\nevent.",[616,669,670,673,674,677],{},[222,671,672],{},"Desk access",": a Website user (customer, supplier portal) given a desk role, which makes them\na System User (",[283,675,676],{},"desk_access",").",[616,679,680,683],{},[222,681,682],{},"Role Profile"," created or granting more roles.",[603,685,526],{"id":686},"weakened-settings",[218,688,689,690,692],{},"A System Settings save raises ",[283,691,520],{}," (critical) when it:",[613,694,695,698,701,704,707],{},[616,696,697],{},"turns off two-factor authentication, the password policy, one session per user, SSO-only login\nor logout on password reset;",[616,699,700],{},"lowers the minimum password score or the lockout duration;",[616,702,703],{},"allows more failed logins, or removes the lockout;",[616,705,706],{},"lengthens sessions;",[616,708,709],{},"lets guests upload files.",[603,711,567],{"id":712},"api-key-used-from-a-new-ip",[218,714,715,716,719,720,723,724,232],{},"Every successful request authenticated by an API key (",[283,717,718],{},"Authorization: token key:secret"," or\n",[283,721,722],{},"Basic",") records the key's address in ",[222,725,726],{},"Wolf API Key IP",[613,728,729,732,738,741],{},[616,730,731],{},"The key's first address, and any address in its first 24 h, form its baseline.",[616,733,734,735,737],{},"After that, an address outside every known \u002F24 (IPv4) or \u002F64 (IPv6) raises ",[283,736,561],{},",\ncritical for privileged users. A new address inside a known network is recorded silently.",[616,739,740],{},"Addresses unused for a year are forgotten. Deleting a row forgets an address.",[616,742,743],{},"The proposed responses are revoking the user's API keys and blocking the address.",[603,745,747],{"id":746},"limits","Limits",[613,749,750,757],{},[616,751,752,753,756],{},"Changes made with raw SQL (a patch, ",[283,754,755],{},"bench mariadb",") fire no document event and are not seen.\nPatches and migrations are skipped on purpose.",[616,758,759,760,763],{},"A User Permission restricted to one DocType (",[283,761,762],{},"applicable_for",") is counted with the user's\nothers for the same allowed DocType.",[234,765,767],{"id":766},"unusual-data-exports","Unusual data exports",[218,769,770,773,774,777,778,232],{},[222,771,772],{},"Wolf Settings → Flag unusual data exports"," (on by default) raises ",[283,775,776],{},"data_exfiltration","\n(T1567, T1030). Preset: ",[295,779,780],{},"Unusual data export",[613,782,783,797,810,831],{},[616,784,785,788,789,792,793,796],{},[222,786,787],{},"What counts",": report exports, Data Export, Data Import templates with records, bulk PDFs,\nand every list read (",[283,790,791],{},"frappe.client.get_list",", the list and report views,\n",[283,794,795],{},"\u002Fapi\u002Fresource\u002F\u003CDocType>","), whatever the page size. A script paging through a table adds up\nlike one big read.",[616,798,799,802,803,806,807,677],{},[222,800,801],{},"How",": the response size of each request counts towards the user's total for the clock\nhour. Every hour, the totals become ",[283,804,805],{},"user_export_bytes"," samples, one series per user\n(",[283,808,809],{},"labels.user",[616,811,812,815,816,819,820,823,824,819,827,830],{},[222,813,814],{},"When",": past ",[222,817,818],{},"Export Floor (MB per hour)"," (default ",[283,821,822],{},"50","), the hour is compared with the\nuser's largest hour over the last 14 days. Warning at ",[222,825,826],{},"Export Factor",[283,828,829],{},"5",") times\nthat hour, critical at 20 times. A user without any history is critical, except while the site\nitself has less than 14 days of history: then it is a warning.",[616,832,833,836],{},[222,834,835],{},"How often",": at most one event per user, hour and severity, so a warning can be followed by\na critical. The payload has the hour's bytes, requests and rows, the baseline, the ratio, the\nlast request and the IP.",[838,839,840],"note",{},[218,841,842,843,845],{},"The ",[283,844,805],{}," series names users. Anyone who may read the site's metrics in Wolf sees\nhow much each user took out per hour.",[218,847,848],{},"Not counted: files sent as they are (private files, backups), printing one document, and the\nfile of a background list export (its request is counted). An export spread across two clock\nhours is split in two. Satellites keep raw samples for 2 days, so their baseline covers 2 days,\nnot 14.",[234,850,339],{"id":851},"geoip-database",[218,853,854,856],{},[295,855,347],{}," needs an offline GeoIP database on the server. Wolf never calls\nan online lookup service.",[858,859,861,865,868,896,900,910,914],"steps",{"level":860},"3",[603,862,864],{"id":863},"download-a-database","Download a database",[218,866,867],{},"Either format works:",[613,869,870,881],{},[616,871,872,873,876,877,880],{},"a MaxMind-format ",[283,874,875],{},".mmdb"," file: GeoLite2-Country or GeoLite2-City (free MaxMind account),\nDB-IP \"IP to Country Lite\" (",[283,878,879],{},"dbip-country-lite-*.mmdb",", CC BY 4.0) or IPinfo Lite. Wolf reads\nit with its own reader, so no extra Python package is needed;",[616,882,883,884,887,888,891,892,895],{},"a CSV of ranges, one per line: ",[283,885,886],{},"start_ip,end_ip,CC"," (DB-IP or IPinfo \"country lite\" CSV),\ninteger ",[283,889,890],{},"start,end,CC,..."," (IP2Location LITE DB1) or ",[283,893,894],{},"network\u002Fprefix,CC",". Header lines are\nskipped.",[603,897,899],{"id":898},"set-the-path","Set the path",[218,901,902,903,906,907,232],{},"Set ",[222,904,905],{},"Wolf Settings → GeoIP Database"," to the file's path. A relative path is read from the site\ndirectory, for example ",[283,908,909],{},"private\u002Ffiles\u002Fdbip-country.mmdb",[603,911,913],{"id":912},"keep-it-fresh","Keep it fresh",[218,915,916],{},"Refresh the file monthly. Wolf reloads it when it changes.",[218,918,919],{},"Private and loopback addresses have no country. A user whose earlier logins all came from such\naddresses has no baseline yet, so nothing is flagged until a first public login is known.",[234,921,923],{"id":922},"turning-a-signal-off","Turning a signal off",[218,925,926,927,929],{},"Untick its switch in ",[222,928,224],{},". On a satellite, the same switches apply to the signals it\nforwards.",{"title":931,"searchDepth":932,"depth":933,"links":934},"",1,2,[935,936,943,944,945],{"id":236,"depth":933,"text":237},{"id":412,"depth":933,"text":413,"children":937},[938,940,941,942],{"id":605,"depth":939,"text":505},3,{"id":686,"depth":939,"text":526},{"id":712,"depth":939,"text":567},{"id":746,"depth":939,"text":747},{"id":766,"depth":933,"text":767},{"id":851,"depth":933,"text":339},{"id":922,"depth":933,"text":923},"Turn on the security signals the Wolf site captures by itself, with no agent, and set up the GeoIP database for new-country logins.","md",null,{},{"icon":122},{"title":119,"description":946},"1NzNxCFzwhzsmQGYU7Vcyghn3Tb5sj5TsRV5glnEhY4",[954,956],{"title":116,"path":112,"stem":113,"description":955,"icon":117},"What Dodock Wolf detects, where each security signal comes from, and how every event is tagged with MITRE ATT&CK.",{"title":124,"path":125,"stem":126,"description":957,"icon":127},"What the Wolf Agent detects in nginx access logs and the auth log, which bench services and site settings it reports as exposed, and which presets alert on them.",1795107943237]